{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death","id":1427347,"title":"What Happens To The Mage's Soul After Death?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-05T05:10:03-08:00","id":1427347,"title":"What Happens To The Mage's Soul After Death?","content":"Well, it's in the title. What happens to an Awakened's soul after death? Do they go to the Underworld/ Shadowlands while their Avatars go for reincarnation, or something else? I haven't opened the books in a while but I don't remember where to read about this, so please, helpeth thy comrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T05:24:21-08:00","id":1427348,"title":"","content":"Different traditions have different views, through it seems like they go through reincarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 12-05-2020, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T05:29:12-08:00","id":1427349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427348#post1427348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different traditions have different views, through it seems like they reincarnation</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T06:31:53-08:00","id":1427356,"title":"","content":"Avatars definitely reincarnate. But souls? Who knows? There's no guarantee they even exist. If they do, do they become ghosts? Maybe. Or maybe ghosts are some sort of residue, a copy of sorts that's made under very specific circumstances that include a person's death. And you don't always get a ghost when a person dies. <br /> <br /> Then there's the matter of a ghost's Transcendence: we don't know what comes next for them if they manage to escape the Shadowlands without succumbing to Oblivion. Is Transcendence merely another kind of Oblivion? Do they ascend to some sort of heaven that's beyond even a Mage's grasp? Do they reincarnate? <br /> <br /> Basically, a long-winded way of saying that no one knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T07:07:11-08:00","id":1427359,"title":"","content":"Since so many things are dependent on paradigm, do Technocrats have souls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T07:43:39-08:00","id":1427366,"title":"","content":"I dont know if this helps, but in the Song of Shadows Dharma book, one of the npc mentors is a former Go Kamisori Gama Ninja Mage, who is assassinated, goes to Yomi and then returns as a Kuei-jin to kill his assassin. So it's likely that Mages can return as Wraiths or Kuei-jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T07:46:43-08:00","id":1427367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427359#post1427359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since so many things are dependent on paradigm, do Technocrats have souls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, there are technocrats that remember being questing knights during the crusades and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T07:48:01-08:00","id":1427368,"title":"","content":"Not much depends on paradigm. Mages souls can and will be reborn (just remember Nefandi and victims of Gilgul).<br /> Mages cannot become ghosts (at least it was said in Euthanatos book) without Mind (astral form) / Spirit (ghoust form) spheres.<br /> Nobody knows WHERE they go. They just reincarnate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427366#post1427366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of the npc mentors is a former Go Kamisori Gama Ninja Mage, who is assassinated, goes to Yomi and then returns as a Kuei-jin to kill his assassin.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I remember, the &quot;east vampires&quot; were heroes in the past who reincarnate and doomed to some kind of punishment because of something in the past.<br /> I think this is a rare event, more related to Kuei-jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-05-2020, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T09:30:23-08:00","id":1427376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427368#post1427368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much depends on paradigm. Mages souls can and will be reborn (just remember Nefandi and victims of Gilgul).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the mage's soul reincarnate, or the Avatar reincarnates bringing memories of its past life? I thought it was the later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T09:49:34-08:00","id":1427377,"title":"","content":"It's the latter. Though whether the Avatar is part of the soul is an open question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T09:54:01-08:00","id":1427378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427376#post1427376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thought it was the later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. The avatar has some independence. However, it is possible to remember past-lifes even without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T10:02:55-08:00","id":1427381,"title":"","content":"Also, the question isn't whether or not a technocrat has a soul. The question is whether or not a technocrat believes she has a soul. Mage says remarkably little about what is actually true concerning the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T10:05:08-08:00","id":1427382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427378#post1427378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both. The avatar has some independence. However, it is possible to remember past-lifes even without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's debatable. Can you confirm that the people who remember past lives aren't remembering them because of a sleeping avatar? (shapeshifters are a special case, because they have their own metaphysics.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T10:50:10-08:00","id":1427384,"title":"","content":"Like most things in Mage, the answer to this is a matter of paradigm. Both the paradigm of the Awakened and the paradigm of the real person interested.<br /> <br /> Within Mage itself there is a great deal of curiosity and uncertainty but my earlier statement aside I\u2019ll try to offer some answers which I hope will be helpful.<br /> <br /> The Avatar seems to be an element of the human soul which is either attached to it or is one part of the gestalt nature of the soul, like an organelle within a cell. We have enough evidence to reasonably conclude that avatars reincarnate and cycle through many Awakened (however perception of this often requires an appropriate paradigm). However, the transmigration and reincarnation of the avatar does not answer the entire question of the fate of the awakened\u2019s soul.<br /> <br /> If the soul is not entirely the avatar, which seems likely to be the case, we can first examine possibilities through looking towards Wraith. There it\u2019s discussed that people with strong attachments to life and memories of the living world can persist as wraiths and with enough luck and willpower even do so lucidly. Given that Awakened can produce wraiths after death but the avatar continue to migrate, we can say then that the part of the Awakened which would remain as a wraith is distinct from the avatar as a representative of the human soul.<br /> <br /> The wraith is capable of Oblivion or Transcendence or seeking residence along the Far Shores. Any one of these could serve as afterlives, nirvana, heaven, hell, or reincarnation depending on the perspective of the individual and given the mysteries involved.<br /> <br /> However wraiths are not the whole of the potential afterlife I think. Given that a small fraction of humans leave wraiths and fewer of those are conscious and all of them are tied to the living world through strong psychic links, it seems unlikely to me that the is the whole of the afterlife.<br /> <br /> As to what else there is? This is one of the mysteries that the WoD leaves and a reason why I say it comes down to a matter of personal paradigm. Any individual can say that there is ultimately something or nothing after death in the WoD and if that\u2019s meaningful to them and their table, that\u2019s valid.<br /> <br /> However, I\u2019m making this post so I should probably posit my own thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> I think a great strength of the WoD\u2019s treatment of death is it\u2019s stance on the mystery. I think leaving what comes after death as the great mystery is a valuable thing. An Awakened\u2019s paradigm dictates what they imagine for themselves after death and perhaps it dictates what they find. Perhaps some Awakened who are thought dead have actually become spirits in a relevant Horizon Realm. Or perhaps they have reentered the cycle of reincarnation. Perhaps they have ceased to be. Perhaps they have gone to the One.<br /> <br /> It may be ultimately impossible to say because paradigm and perspective are the lenses that every individual will see reality through and thus they\u2019ll see it a different way. But I personally like to keep the mystery alive with wisps of suggestion and allusion. Perhaps a Verbena finds themselves receiving visions of Asgard before their death and when they die they are not found within any known Far Shore or Horizon Realm... yet any divinations on the matter dictate they\u2019ve reached their destination. Perhaps the Progenitor who has accepted that they will cease to be after death, once they\u2019ve died, cannot be reached through mystical effort - spirits summoned may take on the Progenitor\u2019s identity but the true spirit, if there is such a thing, has vanished. I perhaps in this one can demonstrate a mystery within the World of Darkness, that one cannot look at Horizon Realms and Farshores as all the mundane other worlds of our (in)finite reality. Such things are great Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:15:26-08:00","id":1427386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427382#post1427382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you confirm that the people who remember past lives aren't remembering them because of a sleeping avatar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you want to say that people do not remember their past life due to the fact that their Avatar is asleep and this blocks their memories? I did not say that. I don't think it (avatar) actively suppresses memories.<br /> <br /> Fairies and werewolves can reincarnate. Fairies remember their lives, werewolves (as far as I remember) do not.<br /> Kuei-jin - I remember they have some discipline (or something else) to see future and past. They seem to be able to receive these visions while they sleep, or am I wrong? After all, they somehow had to understand who they were and what they had lost? I mean, they had a legend that they were Heroes and had some important place in this world.<br /> There is also path of karma that allows our undead friends to see past lives and possible future for someone.<br /> <br /> We have evidence that Avatar is not most important part for reincarnation. However, avatar is active enough to remember and share some information.<br /> I would say that avatar lives separately from mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-05-2020, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:23:34-08:00","id":1427388,"title":"","content":"The Garou and other Changing Breeds are actually a difficult comparison to make here because their situation is so uniquely strange.<br /> <br /> So what was in previous editions called the \u2018Past Lives\u2019 background is now known as the \u2018Ancestors\u2019 background. While all Garou can use rites or umbra leading travel to contact their ancestors, those with the Ancestors background can channel their Ancestors and experience their memories and manifest their skills alongside more readily contacting them. Those Garou with the Pure Breed background also manifest their honored ancestors through both a spiritual and physical resemblance to the heroes of the past.<br /> <br /> This gets even more complex when considering the dual nature of the changing breeds. They are not only human and animal but material and spiritual, not simply the two come together but a gestalt union creating a unique being. While dead changing breeds, particularly those who receive proper death rites and chiniage in the form of ancestor worship will manifest as ancestor-spirits with a presence in the appropriate tribal homelands, there is an element which complicates matters.<br /> <br /> The question of whether the ancestor spirit is the entire spirit of the fallen Garou or if it similar the Fae Soul of the Changeling or the Avatar of the Awakened. The question is if the ancestor spirit is the entirety of the individual\u2019s soul or if there is a human soul which is unique and which departs to whatever awaits humans.<br /> <br /> If anyone can reference or recall a source which discusses if werewolves create wraiths I\u2019d appreciate it but I wouldn\u2019t at all be surprised if we had several contradictory sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:28:07-08:00","id":1427389,"title":"","content":"Fairies and werewolves ability to reincarnate has nothing to do with the human soul. As I said, they have their own metaphysics. <br /> <br /> And no, I'm not saying that a Sleeping Avatar means that the person won't remember it; I'm saying that an Avatar, even if Asleep, could be the channel by which a past life's memories are transmitted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:38:03-08:00","id":1427391,"title":"","content":"(I found an answer in the FAQ within the old Wraith Book Buried Secrets btw - basically Changing Breeds only tend to leave wraiths because of spiritual pollution and Awakened who manifest as wraiths will not have access to their Avatars or Magick)<br /> <br /> That aside, I have to agree, that the unique spiritual circumstances of the Changing Breeds and Changelings, while associated with this discussion, don\u2019t necessarily tell us anything in particular about human souls/spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:52:52-08:00","id":1427394,"title":"","content":"Also, an avatar can be anything you want it to be. By default, you only interact with it as a personality when you are having a seeking. With the circumspect Avatar Merit it may not even take on a personality then. With a manifest avatar merit, it may well be chatting your ear off all the time. Take a manifest Avatar as an ally, and it is able to manifest physically and interact with others. Throw in phylactery, and it is always physically manifest.<br /> <br /> So the spectrum of what the Avatar might be ranges all the way from a completely separate being to a quiet little aspect of your soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:55:01-08:00","id":1427395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427389#post1427389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension Warrior? There are rumors that Avatar was killed, but he returned... or nobody killed him after gilgul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T12:10:47-08:00","id":1427397,"title":"","content":"Rumors that the Avatar was killed. Not the same as proof that it was. In fact, an argument could be made that its reappearance is proof that it wasn't. Assuming that it did reappear and the whole thing wasn't a hoax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-05-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T17:56:58-08:00","id":1427410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427356#post1427356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no guarantee they even exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there is. On Dot 5 of Spirit (S. 524 in German) it is said you need to have this Sphere on this grade if you want create Live that does have a soul.<br /> So the group consens is, that every Ghost is just a Soul without body and unless you are a believer of one of the true ones, your soul will wait until it get to another body.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T18:08:00-08:00","id":1427411,"title":"","content":"Most mages' souls move on somewhere no one knows where.<br /> <br /> A fraction of them get stuck in the Shadowlands<br /> <br /> Just like all the other humans.<br /> <br /> Avatars have their own cycle separate from that, which involves rebirth and carries past life memories.<br /> <br /> I don't really think, speaking from the perspective of an observer reading the fiction, there's any doubt human souls are a thing in the World of Darkness. Mages might have their own theories based on their paradigms and personal beliefs, but there's no reason to assume any kind of complication like &quot;wraiths are just an imprint of someone's personality at the time of death,&quot; and that contradicts other sources anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T05:28:40-08:00","id":1427449,"title":"","content":"There is a Hermetic Mage in the <i>Hidden Lore </i>book, Branwyn Elspeth, and she believes (though this is not stated outright) that she is a reincarnated Mage. Considering she is Arete 4 I don't think that she would hold this belief without it being true.<br /> Edit: Found her. It is written &quot;Branwyn has an old soul - she is a reincarnation of an Order of Hermes magus from the 13th century. She has dreams of her previous life (...) &quot; This is written from the point of view of the narrator, so seems like strong evidence for Mages getting reincarnated to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-06-2020, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T13:11:44-08:00","id":1427485,"title":"","content":"Yeah it seems like both Changlings and werewolves recarnate. So it seems to be that \u201cnormal\u201d souls recarnate to. Like the Changling way in my understanding is when a Changlings mortal vessel dies it goes to the sea of souls and merges with a human soul also recarnateding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T15:57:21-08:00","id":1427497,"title":"","content":"How does it follow from werewolves and changelings reincarnating that humans reincarnate too? I mean, it's <i>possible</i>; but it is far from a certainty.<br /> <br /> In fact, with the shift from Past Lives to Ancestors, there's some question as to whether or not werewolves reincarnate. And even in the case of changelings, it's only the fae aspect that's known to reincarnate. It's possible \u2014 likely, even \u2014 that it separates from the human upon death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T02:22:15-08:00","id":1427539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427497#post1427497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it follow from werewolves and changelings reincarnating that humans reincarnate too? I mean, it's <i>possible</i>; but it is far from a certainty.<br /> <br /> In fact, with the shift from Past Lives to Ancestors, there's some question as to whether or not werewolves reincarnate. And even in the case of changelings, it's only the fae aspect that's known to reincarnate. It's possible \u2014 likely, even \u2014 that it separates from the human upon death.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one needs to guess as to whether anyone reincarnates in the World of Darkness. Wraith 20 page 487 makes it clear some people <i>do.</i> Admittedly, this is a projector background and not technically a Wraith background, but Wraith does at least mention the possibility that of those who immediately move on at death, some might reincarnate. Given that there seems to be evidence of reincarnation in the real world (I'm not saying anything but that there <i>seems to be evidence</i> not saying that it actually happens) it's not much of a stretch to conclude it happens in the World of Darkness. If vampires can be real, the recorded stories of past lives can also be real.<br /> <br /> Interesting stuff, though: <a href=\"https://blogs.scientificamerican.com/bering-in-mind/ian-stevensone28099s-case-for-the-afterlife-are-we-e28098skepticse28099-really-just-cynics/\" target=\"_blank\">https://blogs.scientificamerican.com...y-just-cynics/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T11:37:31-08:00","id":1427618,"title":"","content":"It isn't even clear if everyone has an Avatar or not. Sometimes it seems like the answer is no, but on the flip side one of the explanations for the consensus is the influence of the Avatars of sleepers. <br /> <br /> For what it is worth, I go with the idea that everyone has an Avatar and it is part of the soul, but it may not be a discreet thing so much as a conduit. I prefer the idea that Mages are human, not human plus, but I also think that Avatars with a mythical appearance are really tapped into that mythos. <br /> <br /> As far as the Shadowlands are concerned, my preferred interpretation is that Wraiths are not the complete souls of the departed, just the parts with a deathgrip on life and the parts that want it all to end (the shadow). Most of the soul is pulling towards Transcendence (wherever that goes) and are just waiting till their stuck pieces let go or are torn away by Oblivion. Either way the Avatar isn't active in the Underworld (except, perhaps, as a part of the distant Eidolon) and it isn't at risk of falling into Oblivion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T17:13:35-08:00","id":1427651,"title":"","content":"My preferred interpretation is that wraiths are complete human souls, but avatars are on a different cycle and don't travel with it.<br /> <br /> If wraiths are not complete human souls much of the drama and importance of Wraith itself is significantly undermined. If it's not what it appears to be, then what's the point, really?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T18:53:31-08:00","id":1427662,"title":"","content":"Even in Wraith, is stated, pretty much up front, that they're not\u2026 well, I guess the best way to phrase it would be not all together. Psyche and Shadow are only loosely coupled with each other; Eidolon is very nearly MIA. <br /> <br /> But frankly, this is drifting very much into Wraith territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T05:27:49-08:00","id":1427700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427662#post1427662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in Wraith, is stated, pretty much up front, that they're not\u2026 well, I guess the best way to phrase it would be not all together. Psyche and Shadow are only loosely coupled with each other; Eidolon is very nearly MIA.<br /> <br /> But frankly, this is drifting very much into Wraith territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its kind of hard to discuss Avatars, souls, and the Shadowlands without drifting into Wraith territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T04:20:34-08:00","id":1428332,"title":"","content":"Wraith The Ascension, a diagonal journey. Once, I was a master of reality. Now I am hunted for spare parts. I must build the staircase. Oh, but... damn, my Shadow wrecked it all again. One day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T16:56:26-08:00","id":1428408,"title":"","content":"The question of whether all humans have Avatars is an interesting one. Each person that ever lived received an Avatar? Are Avatars an infinite resource, with as many as necessary, or is there a fixed number? (If Avatars reincarnate, they seem to be limited in number). <br /> <br /> I assume Avatars reincarnate because they still have a reason to, and one could say that reason is to achieve Ascension? So if an Avatar reaches Ascension, a new Avatar takes its place? There are exactly as many Avatars as needed to give one to each human that exists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T17:28:04-08:00","id":1428411,"title":"","content":"Even if Avatars reincarnate, that doesn't mean that they're limited in number; and even if they are, it doesn't mean that that number is less than the total population of humanity. Depending on where Avatars come from and/or where they go between incarnations, there could be a vast, possibly even infinite, pool of Avatars that have never incarnated before. <br /> <br /> And those never before incarnated Avatars are potentially different from brand new Avatars, which are described in the <i>Child Mages</i> section of <b>Book of Secrets</b>: those brand new Avatars are described as having a childlike innocence that manifests, among other things, as True Faith in the Child Mage. By contrast, an Avatar that is old but has never incarnated even once may have lost their innocence in some other way; no one knows what happens to Avatars between (or before) incarnations, and it may well be that guiding and empowering mages isn't the only \u2014 or even the most important \u2014 thing they do. We simply don't know enough one way or the other. <br /> <br /> The reason why Avatars incarnate may be to try for Ascension \u2014 though what Ascension means is also an open question. Is Ascension a way for an Avatar to escape the cycle of reincarnation, or is it a way to transform a mortal human into an Avatar? Or is something else going on? <br /> <br /> Wwe simply don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T17:59:34-08:00","id":1428417,"title":"","content":"I mean, M:tAsc has barely any definition of what ascension could even be wheres M:tAw is fairly straightforward (you get to live permanently in the supernal realm as one of the living symbols that define reality). It's very open-ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T18:05:26-08:00","id":1428419,"title":"","content":"Avatars are aspects of the soul. The Avatar might have different experiences than the rest of the soul, but it is part of the soul. Every normal soul has an Avatar. Some souls have had their Avatars cut off. Gilguld is destroying the Avatar without destroying the soul. <br /> <br /> Most Avatars are deep asleep. And it can be brutal and spiritually mutilating to force an Avatar awake. Or that's my take from reading most of the Mage source and rule books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T08:31:46-08:00","id":1428477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1428419#post1428419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatars are aspects of the soul. The Avatar might have different experiences than the rest of the soul, but it is part of the soul. Every normal soul has an Avatar. Some souls have had their Avatars cut off. Gilguld is destroying the Avatar without destroying the soul.<br /> <br /> Most Avatars are deep asleep. And it can be brutal and spiritually mutilating to force an Avatar awake. Or that's my take from reading most of the Mage source and rule books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Masters of the Art</i> book notes in the Spirit 9 capability of Awaken Avatar that a forced Awakening might cause the person to be deranged, or the Avatar to be damaged.<br /> <br /> In regard to Gilgul - it is written on page 47 of the Order of Hermes Revised book that the Rote of Gilgul is poorly understood, and it might very well be dismissing the soul (the Avatar?) of the Mage to another plane, there to wait for judgement. Makes sense to me, I always thought it was over the top that an Avatar could be destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-19-2020, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T22:59:47-08:00","id":1428989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427662#post1427662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in Wraith, is stated, pretty much up front, that they're not\u2026 well, I guess the best way to phrase it would be not all together. Psyche and Shadow are only loosely coupled with each other; Eidolon is very nearly MIA.<br /> <br /> But frankly, this is drifting very much into Wraith territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be complete while also being divergent. Wraith doesn't say they're incomplete, it just names the psyche, shadow, and eidolon as you mentioned. Although, Wraith 20 says the eidolon is usually firmly integrated with the wraith's psyche, and that it only manifests as a separate entity at higher levels. It's not so much missing as it's a part of the wraith that can cope better with the shadow.<br /> <br /> What I mean is that I see no reason to assume that anything in particular is missing, and that having significant pieces missing undermines Wraith's themes in that you're not really the person who died so what does your existence mean?<br /> <br /> And in a thread about what happens to mages when they die, Wraith seems fairly relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T07:06:07-08:00","id":1429024,"title":"","content":"As has been stated, the canon does leaves this mistery open.<br /> <br /> Personaly, in my headcanon about this topic I do think mages can leave a ghost (it's ever stated that they can't?), and in that case relate the Avatar with the Eidolon - particularly at higher levels. As both seem to seek a form of trascendence. I also like <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_(WOD)#Mummies\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy's way</a> of seeing the soul, that includes the body as part of it.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the sepparation of the different parts of the soul should be treated as a big deal. I think Wraith mentions somewhere that the underworld it's a place, but can also be seen as a reflection of the spiritual journey of the individual wraith. If such a big an populated scenarion can be also seen as a sort of &quot;individual seeking&quot;, it's not so hard to think that different parts of your soul can be in different places, yet it's still all you and your journey - Heck Mages with Correspondence 4 can easily show that such divides may be a matter of perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-19-2020, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T06:13:31-08:00","id":1429349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1428989#post1428989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I mean is that I see no reason to assume that anything in particular is missing, and that having significant pieces missing undermines Wraith's themes in that you're not really the person who died so what does your existence mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Missing, no. Checked out, yes. You can already see it with the Shadow and the Psyche. They are both the person in question, with all the memories and identity, but they are expressed through different lenses. Specifically the two lenses that most resist Transcendence.<br /> <br /> The Avatar is likely to be one of the first aspects to check out as it is always less focused on regular life than on Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 12-21-2020, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T01:40:27-08:00","id":1429927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1428411#post1428411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And those never before incarnated Avatars are potentially different from brand new Avatars, which are described in the <i>Child Mages</i> section of <b>Book of Secrets</b>: those brand new Avatars are described as having a childlike innocence that manifests, among other things, as True Faith in the Child Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds super interesting. How did this true faith play out in practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T03:42:18-08:00","id":1429928,"title":"","content":"The book suggests that, like innocence, it tends not to survive contact with the World of Darkness: in adults, True Faith is generally accompanied by a strong code of ethics designed to preserve it, and it's really ready to deviate from that code and to lose the True Faith. Basically, it's treated as something that's easily lost unless you're meticulously self-disciplined and very careful to avoid losing it. <br /> <br /> Children are not known for being meticulously self-disciplined or very careful. <br /> <br /> As such, the True Faith of a child with a new soul tends to be a very fleeting thing, and will usually be gone before you know it. If protagonist characters weren't an exception to statistical truths, the typical \u201cnew soul\u201d character would be one where the True Faith is part of her backstory, along with an event describing how she lost it. Statistically, it's not something you <i>have</i>; is something you <i>had</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T06:19:15-08:00","id":1429936,"title":"","content":"I always wondered if the avatar is the soul, part of the soul, or some independent spirit that attaches to a person. Werewolf seems to suggest it is a spirit as Shapechangers can attack and eat avatars. The Avatar cannot be the soul as Vampires are described as still having souls and can even become ghosts, but being embraced destroys the avatar. <br /> <br /> It seems that it may be just part of a person's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T20:26:19-08:00","id":1435146,"title":"","content":"Which Werewolf book says shapeshifters can eat Avatars? I'm not saying you're wrong, I just haven't read it. There is an Ahadi Gift in W20 Changing-Breeds that lets them permanently destroy a spirit or ghost, preventing it from ever reforming. (Appropriately it's named Ghost-Eating Technique, after the nearly identical Charm in Exalted.) But it doesn't mention Avatars, so I guess you decide whether an Avatar count as a spirit in your WoD.<br /> <br /> (Considering that spirits automatically reform after you kill them, it's pretty weird that the Garou have never tried to learn this Gift before. Haven't they realized that war against Banes is <i>pointless</i> without Ghost-Eating? Silly dogs.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1427449#post1427449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Hermetic Mage in the <i>Hidden Lore </i>book, Branwyn Elspeth, and she believes (though this is not stated outright) that she is a reincarnated Mage. Considering she is Arete 4 I don't think that she would hold this belief without it being true.<br /> Edit: Found her. It is written &quot;Branwyn has an old soul - she is a reincarnation of an Order of Hermes magus from the 13th century. She has dreams of her previous life (...) &quot; This is written from the point of view of the narrator, so seems like strong evidence for Mages getting reincarnated to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what about the time in-between the 13th and 20th centuries? Was she a very long-lived Hermetic, or was she a Sleeper in-between, or was her Avatar just not incarnated anywhere in-between? Do Avatars reincarnate instantly, or does it take them a while to be reborn?<br /> <br /> Is it usual for Mages to remember past lives? I had gotten the impression that normally only the Akashics and Euthanatoi made a habit of remembering their past lives. Is it just more common for them, or does it happen equally to all kinds of Mages?<br /> <br /> Do Avatars normally reincarnate in the same paradigm and Tradition every time? Again, I get the impression Akashics and Euthanatoi never &quot;change sides&quot; and that was what made the Himalayan war so long and senseless.<br /> <br /> If Technocrats can remember past lives, doesn't that clash utterly with the usual Technocratic BS about souls not existing? Do they just ignore/rationalize the cognitive dissonance because of their Conditioning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-10-2021, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T05:38:02-08:00","id":1435178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435146#post1435146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do Avatars reincarnate instantly, or does it take them a while to be reborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like most things on this thread, this is largely unknown.<br /> <br /> It's said that Avatars have to go trough the Wheel of Souls (in the high umbra) to purify before reincarnating, this migth take a while. In the Himalayan Wars, however, it seems like Avatars of the slain would quickly return to get vengeance.<br /> <br /> I would say that in some cases it could take a while, in others it could be instant. Perhaps depending on the Avatar, it's own baggage and agendas, and those of their previous life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it usual for Mages to remember past lives? I had gotten the impression that normally only the Akashics and Euthanatoi made a habit of remembering their past lives. Is it just more common for them, or does it happen equally to all kinds of Mages? </div> </div> </div> It does seem to be more common among mages that believe in reincarnation.<br /> <br /> But that could be less a quality of the Avatar itself, and more a consequence of such mages actively *searching* their souls for past lives. Perhaps most Avatars can access some information of past lives, but most mages simply don't care about developping this potential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do Avatars normally reincarnate in the same paradigm and Tradition every time? Again, I get the impression Akashics and Euthanatoi never &quot;change sides&quot; and that was what made the Himalayan war so long and senseless. </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Technocrats have a Defect that consists in having a mystical Avatar that pushes them towards deviance. So we know they can reincarnate on mages with wildly different Paradigms But, of course, this isn't common. Usually the Avatar doesn't influence the Paradigm of the Mage.<br /> <br /> While this *migth* be a hint of Aatars usualy reincarnating on the same Paradigm, it could also hint that most Avatars don't care much about factions and such.<br /> <br /> Avatars are supposed to guide mages towards further enligthenment and Ascencion, it doesn't make a lot of sense for them to be too concerned with such issues - that are often regarded as obstacles and traps.<br /> <br /> But Avatars aren't perfect. They can get addict to vampire blood, they can be broken and inverted. Many supernatural Defects can be seen as the consequence of having a flawed Avatar. I would take the Himalayan Wars as the Avatars being overcomed by karmic baggage<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Technocrats can remember past lives, doesn't that clash utterly with the usual Technocratic BS about souls not existing? Do they just ignore/rationalize the cognitive dissonance because of their Conditioning? </div> </div> </div>Avatars ARE a spicy subject for Technocrats.<br /> <br /> But you should never underestimate the power of technobabble and scy-fy nonsense theories, they probably have an explanation for Past Lives somewhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T15:45:59-08:00","id":1435253,"title":"","content":"I'd say that Akashics and Euthanatoi might be more likely than the average mage to <i>imbue</i> their avatars with either the desire or the destiny to continue their current work/philosophy/fight in the next incarnation. I don't see the Hermetics or Sons of Ether, for example, as being particularly likely to attempt such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T05:06:15-08:00","id":1435285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435253#post1435253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that Akashics and Euthanatoi might be more likely than the average mage to <i>imbue</i> their avatars with either the desire or the destiny to continue their current work/philosophy/fight in the next incarnation. I don't see the Hermetics or Sons of Ether, for example, as being particularly likely to attempt such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>More likely to imbue their avatars for the next generation, or more likely to look at the philosophy/work/fight their avatars did in past lives? The latter seems more likely than the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T18:23:24-08:00","id":1435331,"title":"","content":"Probably, but I was speaking to the tendency of the mages to join the same Tradition as their avatar's past lives. Once you know enough to look back into past lives like that, you're probably already well established in a Tradition that values doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T19:05:30-08:00","id":1435334,"title":"","content":"Personally, I prefer treating the various Avatar related merits and flaws as being at least correlated with the mage's Focus. There can be exceptions to this (the recently cited Technocracy-specific Flaw is <i>by definition</i> an exception to this, and one that I generalize as \u201cyour Avatar loathes your Focus\u201d); but for the most part, I prefer the notion that the Avatar either tends to be compatible with the Mage's belief system (you're not going to have an Avatar providing access to Past Lives if the mage in question doesn't believe in Past Lives; or is it vice versa?) or is somehow constrained by the mage's beliefs (a mage with a belief system that doesn't allow for Past Lives supresses her Avatar's ability to impart visions of any past lives it happens to have). <br /> <br /> Again, there would be exceptions; but for the most part, Foci that involve the notion of reincarnation will tend to have the lion's share of Past Lives; and Technocratic Geniuses are more likely to be Circumspect than most Avatars. That sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T07:24:21-08:00","id":1435358,"title":"","content":"So are these glimpses of past lives not possible until the Mage starts actively looking for them with Seekings or Spirit or Time? Or can someone start seeing Past Lives in dreams or Seekings even without looking for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T07:36:05-08:00","id":1435359,"title":"","content":"You have to go looking for it, but it doesn't require a Seeking or Spheres; just the Past Lives Background and meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T08:51:50-08:00","id":1435361,"title":"","content":"My own personal headcanon is that Avatar and Soul are one and the same and the whole thing reincarnates.<br /> <br /> A Wraith can\u2019t work Magick for the same reason a vampire or Sleeper can\u2019t; Magick requires the soul to be in a particular state of being. Specifically it seems the soul must be tied to a specific living pattern that quintessence flows freely through... versus a vampiric corpse which is a static pool of quintessence that is only refueled by sucking more out of living beings or a bodiless soul that only refuels off the memories and emotions of others. Werewolves and Fae are basically soul/spirit hybrids that result in their only being able to channel quintessence in accord with their spirit\u2019s nature.<br /> <br /> Sleepers have the same soul state as a Mage, just not conscious access to it so it exerts a general pressure against that which it doesn\u2019t believe in. This is why their disbelief causes pushback against vulgar Magick while supernaturals whose souls aren\u2019t linked up in the same way don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> As to what happens to a soul/avatar (Awake or Sleeping), I think the very nature of WoD\u2019s cosmology is set up such that reincarnation is the default. That\u2019s the whole triatic cycle; birth, life, death, birth again. As Orpheus posits; even Oblivion itself is a lie; it all gets recycled eventually.<br /> <br /> Wraiths are just stuck on one part of the cycle and the main difference between Transcendence and Oblivion is how much you retain on your next spin through the cycle (those who transcend recycle with important aspects of themselves intact, key personality traits, desires, spiritual connections, submerged memories... Oblivion instead wipes all those away and results in having to start over from scratch).<br /> <br /> So a Mage who becomes a Wraith isn\u2019t going to see someone else pop up with their recycled avatar; their soul/avatar is busy being a Wraith. Only once they\u2019ve Transcended (in which case their next life will have strong links to their previous ones) or met Oblivion (in which case their soul starts again fresh in the next life) can their soul/avatar be reborn in a new mortal body.<br /> <br /> Ascension is leaving the whole cycle behind for whatever is beyond it. This might be what a Christian recognizes as Heaven/Union with God. It might instead be the ability to spawn your own new Creation in accord with your Will or the Transcendence of Nonbeing... regardless it\u2019s something beyond even Awakened comprehension.*<br /> <br /> * Heck, leave aside the concept of linear time and the entire WoD and everyone in it might be the countless journeys of a single soul through the cycles until it can finally know itself so completely that it can ascend/move on to its next thought experiment (i.e. not only are we all gods, we\u2019re all the same God endeavoring to know Itself better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T09:17:55-08:00","id":1435363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435361#post1435361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Orpheus posits; even Oblivion itself is a lie; it all gets recycled eventually.<br /> <br /> Wraiths are just stuck on one part of the cycle and the main difference between Transcendence and Oblivion is how much you retain on your next spin through the cycle (those who transcend recycle with important aspects of themselves intact, key personality traits, desires, spiritual connections, submerged memories... Oblivion instead wipes all those away and results in having to start over from scratch).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I saw something hinted like this in Book of Worlds (the only Mage book I have*). I'll have to reread it. So Oblivion is more like the River Lethe in Greek Myth, and less like utter nonbeing/destruction?<br /> <br /> *wait no I have 2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-14-2021, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T13:49:46-08:00","id":1435391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435363#post1435363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I saw something hinted like this in Book of Worlds (the only Mage book I have). I'll have to reread it. So Oblivion is more like the River Lethe in Greek Myth, and less like utter nonbeing/destruction?</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>could</i> be. I've not looked at End Game in quite a while, but here's a re-post from another thread that dealt with Oblivion and the larger WoD cosmology which sums up part of it;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main way I dealt with it in my Mage campaign was to take one of the elements of Orpheus and run with it; Oblivion is a LIE. The idea that all of Creation can be undone is the Nephandic equivalent of a fairy tale. In one campaign the PCs were investigating and ended up on the edge of Oblivion itself... specifically at the spiritual embodiment of the Fallen Tower which was a Nephandic holy site that leaned out over the maw of Oblivion). What they learned through ancient writings on the walls is that the Oblivion was a myth created by the first Neverborn Malfeans... the first beings to reach its edge and falter in primal fear at the gateway to the unknown. This myth of eternal destruction filtered up to other spirits of the dead and the practices of Mages who associated with the dead and over time was corrupted by angry outcast mages into a nihilistic credo that became the first Nephandi.<br /> <br /> It filtered up to the Fera as well in the story that the Primeval Wyrm had gone insane and was now consuming everything.<br /> <br /> The Nephandic Cauls, the Black Spiral, the Banes and corruption spirits all grew from the power of belief in this lie and further hiding the truth.<br /> <br /> The Truth? Oblivion/the Wyrm is what it has always been... the portal to birth/rebirth and the transition from one life to the next. The primal fear of the Neverborn is the fear of an infant being born from the safety of a mother\u2019s womb that is all it has ever known into a bright, cold uncertain world beyond.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn are literally the \u201cnever born.\u201d Primeval miscarriages whose spirits were too afraid of birth and even more terrified of the unknowns of rebirth to pass through \u201cOblivion\u2019s\u201d maw.<br /> <br /> The greatest irony is that the corruption the werewolves are fighting isn\u2019t actually the Wyrm at all. It\u2019s just the natural side effect of the Weaver\u2019s efforts to keep the current world from sliding into the maw of Rebirth.<br /> <br /> By defying the natural pull of entropy, the Wraith Hierarchy, the Weaver Spirits (embodying man\u2019s primal desire for a stable and knowable world... a fear of chaos and the unknown), the static vampires and the Technocracy all must build ever more elaborate constructs and schemes to keep it from all tumbling down... and it is the imperfections in this ever more rickety structure and compromises needed to keep it all afloat that creates the corruption the werewolves sense as The Wyrm.<br /> <br /> What the werewolves are actually fighting is not the True Wyrm, but the corruption in the construct built by Man to protect itself from the very primal fears of corruption/oblivion placed in them by the Impergium. The Nephandi are lunatics who drive themselves insane because their exposure to \u201cThe Truth\u201d instills in them not a desire to clear away the rot so there\u2019s room for new growth, but a nihilistic desire to \u201ctear it all down.\u201d<br /> <br /> Both the Banes and the Nephandi are self-destructive messes because they are NOT actually any sort of cosmic force of oblivion.<br /> <br /> The banes the werewolves fight are the natural corruption of a system that has grown too stagnant (like papering over the dry rot or applying another layer of bondo and paint to the rust on a car), but corruption keeps growing because the wolves are so focused on the symptoms, they can\u2019t see the disease (i.e. the stagnation of the world) and even more that THEY are actually the root cause of that disease (the world stagnates because of its overwhelming fear of the unknown... of the monsters that lurk there and prey upon them... in short, the werewolves from days past).<br /> <br /> The Nephandi are the people who react to a cancer diagnosis by trying to kill themselves to just get it over with instead of devoting the time and energy it would take to actually cleanse the body of the poisons.<br /> <br /> In other words, the actual means of restoring the cosmic balance is to stop fighting \u201cOblivion\u201d (or to reach Transcendence, which is the same thing except you're able to bring a few important things with you to the next cycle) and allow the dead and corrupt to be consumed so they can be reborn. The Wyrm and Nephandi are just the two opposite extremes of dealing with it (\u201cignore it and hope it goes away\u201d and \u201cburn it all down\u201d respectively).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T22:19:14-08:00","id":1435424,"title":"","content":"Huh. That's interesting Chris, especially about the Neverborn. I agree with your view of the Impergium, but you've misunderstood or missed how Werewolf depicts the Triat. I don't want to derail the thread, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435334#post1435334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I prefer treating the various Avatar related merits and flaws as being at least correlated with the mage's Focus. There can be exceptions to this (the recently cited Technocracy-specific Flaw is <i>by definition</i> an exception to this, and one that I generalize as \u201cyour Avatar loathes your Focus\u201d); but for the most part, I prefer the notion that the Avatar either tends to be compatible with the Mage's belief system (you're not going to have an Avatar providing access to Past Lives if the mage in question doesn't believe in Past Lives; or is it vice versa?) or is somehow constrained by the mage's beliefs (a mage with a belief system that doesn't allow for Past Lives supresses her Avatar's ability to impart visions of any past lives it happens to have).<br /> <br /> Again, there would be exceptions; but for the most part, Foci that involve the notion of reincarnation will tend to have the lion's share of Past Lives; and Technocratic Geniuses are more likely to be Circumspect than most Avatars. That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any Mystick Paradigms that don't accept reincarnation, at least of Avatars? It seems to be an incontrovertible fact of the setting, anyway. I can see why some Paradigms might consider reincarnation unimportant (&quot;who cares?&quot;, asks the stereotypical Hermetic, Technomancer, or power-hungry jerk) or believe it only involves the Avatar while the rest of the soul become an ancestor spirit or goes to Heaven or Hell. But it's hard to argue Avatars <b>don't</b> reincarnate when there're so many who remember past lives, and truly new Avatars are noticeably different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T06:34:18-08:00","id":1435446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435424#post1435424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. That's interesting Chris, especially about the Neverborn. I agree with your view of the Impergium, but you've misunderstood or missed how Werewolf depicts the Triat. I don't want to derail the thread, though.<br /> <br /> Are there any Mystick Paradigms that don't accept reincarnation, at least of Avatars? It seems to be an incontrovertible fact of the setting, anyway. I can see why some Paradigms might consider reincarnation unimportant (&quot;who cares?&quot;, asks the stereotypical Hermetic, Technomancer, or power-hungry jerk) or believe it only involves the Avatar while the rest of the soul become an ancestor spirit or goes to Heaven or Hell. But it's hard to argue Avatars <b>don't</b> reincarnate when there're so many who remember past lives, and truly new Avatars are noticeably different.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Among extremely diverse Traditions like the Dreamspeakers or the Celestial Chorus, there would have to be some that rejected reincarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T06:54:16-08:00","id":1435449,"title":"","content":"The Past Lives Background calls out the Celestial Chorus and the Technocracy in particular as factions that don't believe in reincarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T10:03:09-08:00","id":1435464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435449#post1435449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Past Lives Background calls out the Celestial Chorus and the Technocracy in particular as factions that don't believe in reincarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd agree that most of the Chorus wouldn't believe in reincarnation but as some monotheists, do believe in reincarnation, some of the Chorus must embrace reincarnation. This includes some Christians as well. Many Christians have believed in reincarnation including several of the men who taught Saint Augustine Theology.<br /> <br /> Similarly, since the Dreamspeakers started as a catchall for small scale non-European societies, an amazingly wide category, and one that includes several groups that don't believe in reincarnation, some Dreamspeakers must reject reincarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-14-2021, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T11:29:44-08:00","id":1435471,"title":"","content":"Obviously, no generalization about any group is absolutely true. Including this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T06:45:46-08:00","id":1435552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435391#post1435391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main way I dealt with it in my Mage campaign was to take one of the elements of Orpheus and run with it; Oblivion is a LIE. The idea that all of Creation can be undone is the Nephandic equivalent of a fairy tale. In one campaign the PCs were investigating and ended up on the edge of Oblivion itself... specifically at the spiritual embodiment of the Fallen Tower which was a Nephandic holy site that leaned out over the maw of Oblivion). What they learned through ancient writings on the walls is that the Oblivion was a myth created by the first Neverborn Malfeans... the first beings to reach its edge and falter in primal fear at the gateway to the unknown. This myth of eternal destruction filtered up to other spirits of the dead and the practices of Mages who associated with the dead and over time was corrupted by angry outcast mages into a nihilistic credo that became the first Nephandi.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The Truth? Oblivion/the Wyrm is what it has always been... the portal to birth/rebirth and the transition from one life to the next. The primal fear of the Neverborn is the fear of an infant being born from the safety of a mother\u2019s womb that is all it has ever known into a bright, cold uncertain world beyond.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The headcanon I posted earlier is sort of similar. With the Psyche and Shadow as the tethers that keep the soul from Transcending, if they fall to Oblivion the soul is cut free to Transcend. Oblivion really is a destructive and annihilative force- it isn't a gateway to anything- but what it eats are the things that keep souls from passing through the real gateway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T21:07:00-08:00","id":1436936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1435552#post1435552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The headcanon I posted earlier is sort of similar. With the Psyche and Shadow as the tethers that keep the soul from Transcending, if they fall to Oblivion the soul is cut free to Transcend. Oblivion really is a destructive and annihilative force- it isn't a gateway to anything- but what it eats are the things that keep souls from passing through the real gateway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the soul just loses their Passions and Fetters, or that they actually lose the psyche and shadow? Do they receive new ones somehow? If not, how could such a damaged soul reincarnate? It seems like it would require the Spell of Life with multiple Tem-Akhu before it'd be viable again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T05:30:43-08:00","id":1436978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1427347-what-happens-to-the-mage-s-soul-after-death?p=1436936#post1436936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean the soul just loses their Passions and Fetters, or that they actually lose the psyche and shadow? Do they receive new ones somehow? If not, how could such a damaged soul reincarnate? It seems like it would require the Spell of Life with multiple Tem-Akhu before it'd be viable again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the Psyche and Shadow don't really present any element of the soul as an eternal reincarnating thing, instead they represent aspects and memories of the most recent life. That leaves a lot of room for headcanon about what they are and how important to the overall integrity of the soul they are. Is the psyche the part of the soul that interfaces with the world, or is it the shape that part of the soul takes on in this life?<br /> <br /> The way I view it, the Psyche and Shadow are specifically just the parts of the soul that don't want to move on, either because they don't want to let go or they don't want to continue at all. That's why, although they have the complete memories of life, certain emotions (Passions) and things (Fetters) eclipse everything else. Most of the soul, including the Avatar and Eidolon, has checked out, we are playing as the obsessive and self destructive parts that haven't. The Psyche and Shadow are not complete organs of the soul, they are like skin that has grown into a bandage or the thorns on a burweed seed. If they are torn off the soul loses character but not integrity. Much of the uniqueness and personality of the most recent life is lost.<br /> <br /> I don't want to portray the Psyche and Shadow as if they don't matter. In a game that focuses on identity, like Wraith does, that loss is of paramount importance. If they die the loss matters and the change that is forced on the soul matters, but the soul only changes it does not reduce.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T18:27:15-08:00","id":1437065,"title":"","content":"Thanks for clarifying. That is a new interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}